-- title:
--   Length of a-torsion in 𝒪/𝔪ⁿ⁺¹ bounded by ℓ(𝒪/(a))
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain and a discrete valuation ring (so in particular local, with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m =$ `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪`), let $a \in \mathcal O$ be arbitrary, and let $n$ be a natural number. Consider the $\mathcal O$-module $\mathcal O/\mathfrak m^{n+1}$ and the $\mathcal O$-linear endomorphism given by multiplication by $a$, i.e. `LinearMap.lsmul 𝒪 (𝒪 ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪 ^ (n + 1)) a`. The assertion is the inequality, in $\mathbb N \cup \{\infty\}$, of module lengths
--   $$\ell_{\mathcal O}\bigl(\ker(a \colon \mathcal O/\mathfrak m^{n+1} \to \mathcal O/\mathfrak m^{n+1})\bigr) \le \ell_{\mathcal O}\bigl(\mathcal O/(a)\bigr),$$
--   where the right-hand side is the length of the quotient of $\mathcal O$ by the ideal generated by the single element $a$. No hypothesis is imposed on $a$: for $a = 0$ the right-hand side is $\infty$ and for $a$ a unit both sides are $0$, and the exponent is written as $n+1$ so that the modulus is a positive power of $\mathfrak m$.
--
--   This is the elementary length count underlying the bound on the $a$-torsion of a truncated discrete valuation ring, $(\mathcal O/\mathfrak m^{n+1})[a] \cong \mathcal O/\mathfrak m^{\min(v(a),\,n+1)}$. It is used by [`GaloisRep.DeformationRingData.length_level_quotient_le_of_ordinaryLine`](thm.html#GaloisRep.DeformationRingData.length_level_quotient_le_of_ordinaryLine) to bound the length of a quotient of a level ring attached to a deformation problem.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDiscreteValuationRing_length_ker_lsmul_quotient_maximalIdeal_pow_le.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
